From 5e881c4237d7272d5d9bd649be8b1d8b4d0f8104 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Seyoon Ragavan <complexzetaprime@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 00:21:20 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] The phase host's remaining reads through its published
 equations
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Twelve older proofs in seven files read phaseHostTM by its definition: the
start state, the redirect branch's dispatch, single table reads, and NDHost's
phaseHostND_fixChoice. Each now reads the host only through
phaseHostTM_q₀, phaseHostTM_tr_of_red_some and phaseHostTM_tr_of_red_none;
every file elaborates with phaseHostTM irreducible, and no proof passes it to
simp. Statements unchanged.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
